      },
      "lineNbr": 62,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003935
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-05T14:23:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This was a bit tricky.\n\nA verifier should always have a ref state. Only when a verifier was update we created the updated Verifier instance in VerifierConfig.onSave at a point where we didn\u0027t know the new SHA1 yet, hence in this case the ref state was not set. I fixed this in VerifierConfig by builder the updated verifier config only after the commit has been written. This means the ref state here in Verifier no longer needs to be optional.\n\nDone.",
      "parentUuid": "c2ca16b8_f2022169",
      "revId": "f3551f2bbb2422ac4b51f728fdbf39b1f195af45",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153",
      "unresolved": false
    },
